  source-request-preflight
    role source-request-preflight
    defined-by relation
    definition "One occurrence of every registered request role binds the entire unquoted request to maintained declaration, goal, Read history, import graph, protected-byte and accepted-operation contracts."
    precondition "The complete request has paired quotes, exact technical operands, no unknown independent clauses, complete prerequisite Reads, an absent owned destination and byte-exact private host source receipts."
    effect "Authorizes only a leased reversible candidate. Delivery additionally requires the actual candidate digest before and after the accepted operation, unchanged protected inputs and an owned zero exit status. Unknown imported initialization and caller effects remain conditional; absence of proof refuses or rolls back only unchanged owned bytes."
    unit "not applicable"
    example "An observed optional-record producer and text consumer compose through imports under a null guard; an outside deployment demand prevents the candidate write."
