  null
    role null
    defined-by relation
    definition "The JavaScript null primitive is the exact absence value established by a source IR literal or guard. It is distinct from undefined, false and an empty record."
    precondition "The observed producer conditional IR proves null absence; the emitter and checker use that same primitive."
    effect "Preserves the proved absent branch; no imported initializer or arbitrary caller effect is certified."
    unit "not applicable"
    example "A source-qualified optional result is absent as null or is rendered by the observed consumer; unknown structure refuses."
    lexeme en
      words "null absence"
    lexeme ru
      words "отсутствие null"
    lexeme hi
      words "null अनुपस्थिति"
    lexeme zh
      words "null 缺失值"
    lexeme es
      words "ausencia null"
  optional-record
    role optional-record
    defined-by relation
    definition "A conditional schema that admits one source-qualified record or the explicit null absence value, with source-derived fields and preconditions."
    precondition "Actual source contracts bind the record fields and absent branch; unknown getters, Proxy objects and unproved structural inputs retain refusal."
    effect "Binds compatible producer result and consumer input under the verified schema conditions, without universal runtime purity."
    unit "not applicable"
    example "A source-qualified optional result is absent as null or is rendered by the observed consumer; unknown structure refuses."
    lexeme en
      words "optional source record"
    lexeme ru
      words "необязательная исходная запись"
