  source-contract-diagnostic
    role source-contract-diagnostic
    defined-by relation
    definition "Authored diagnostic surfaces report the exact unsatisfied source-contract condition in the selected language."
    precondition "A unique source-bound diagnostic code and one declared language select exactly one nonempty surface; a missing or ambiguous record refuses rendering."
    effect "Returns seed text only. Rendering does not consume a Goal or Need, authorize Read or Write, prove purity, accept a receipt, or certify execution."
    unit "diagnostic text"
    example "A source URL mismatch reports the corresponding condition while its import ownership remains refused."
